Types of Multi-Agent Systems
-----------------------------

| Type                      | Description                                                                            | Communication Style           | Example                                                                      |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Sequential Chat Agent** | Agents work one after another. The output of one agent becomes the input for the next. | One after another             | Planner → Search → Booking → Payment                                         |
| **Joint Chat Agent**      | All agents work together simultaneously and contribute equally to solve the task.      | Equal contribution            | Research team where all agents analyze together                              |
| **Group Chat Agent**      | One manager coordinates several specialized agents and combines their outputs.         | Group Manager + Group Members | Project Manager Agent coordinating Coding, Testing, and Documentation Agents |
| **Hierarchical Agent**    | A master agent assigns tasks to subordinate agents and controls the overall workflow.  | Master–Slave hierarchy        | CEO Agent managing Finance, HR, and Sales Agents                             |


